# Agent Design and Evaluation

COMP 4991 Independent Study, Fall 2026 · Mallory Berg · Advisor: Dr. Sean Connin
Working title: *Can Agents Ask the Right Questions?*

## What this is

A reproducible evaluation harness that scores a deliberately simple, hand-coded agent on whether it asks, answers, or abstains correctly when given natural-language data requests against a governed, synthetic data dictionary. The harness is the product. The agent is the subject under test and stays as simple as I can keep it, so that what gets measured is the measurement itself.

The system: one hand-coded agent with a tool loop on the raw API, and a single-turn baseline that cannot ask as the control. No orchestration, no framework, no UI, no fine-tuning.

## Status (as of Oct 25, 2026)

Done: environment (Postgres in Docker Compose, self-seeding synthetic database, read-only `agent_reader` role); baseline run on five requests with JSONL logs; data dictionary v1 with five labeled ambiguity dimensions; eval set v1 (30 tasks, labeled ask / answer / abstain); second-rater pass on 15 tasks; agent v1 running end to end on the five baseline requests with trajectory logs.

Next: gold SQL and the methodology write-up, then harness v1.

## Where things are

- `compose.yaml` and `db/` — the database. `docker compose up` builds and seeds it.
- `db_sql.py` — shared read-only database connection used by both scripts.
- `baseline.py` — the single-turn control.
- `agent_v1.py` — the agent: five tools, system prompt in `system_prompt.txt`, flow in `docs/agent_v1_flowchart.md`.
- `data_dictionary_v0.txt` / `data_dictionary_v1.txt` — the dictionary versions the baseline and agent read.
- `validation_lookup.csv` — published figures the agent checks aggregates against.
- `logs/` — JSONL records, one per run (`baseline_runs.jsonl`, `agent_runs.jsonl`).
- Both scripts need a `.env` with the database connection values and an OpenRouter API key (not in the repo).
- The shared folder holds the study plan, definition of done, eval set, checkpoint documents, and status notes.
- At each checkpoint, one document in the shared folder and one tag on this repository carry the same name.

